--- body ---
## Context

The last step of 0942: once every consumer resolves at point of use, remove the
credential-loading half of `bash-env.sh` so nothing is resident any more.

Blocked by 0943 and 0944, its real prerequisites -- NOT by the 0942 tracker.
Landing this first would break every consumer that still reads the ambient
environment.

What remains of `bash-env.sh` afterwards is the project `.env` strict-parse and
the protected-name refusal, which are worth keeping and are independently
tested. The 0939 xtrace guard becomes vestigial for credentials but still
covers whatever the strict-parse assigns; decide at implementation time whether
to keep it, and say which in the commit message.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `bash-env.sh` no longer sources or exports any keystore provider file
- [ ] `KEYS=` handling is REMOVED OUTRIGHT -- decided by the author 2026-09-16.
      No no-op, no deprecation shim: a residual inert `KEYS=` line would read
      as configuration that still does something. The `.env` line goes too.
- [ ] `bash -x -c ':'` exposes no credential value (names-only probe, as in 0939)
- [ ] `/proc/<pid>/environ` of a fresh child carries no credential
- [ ] Every existing bash-env suite is updated or retired deliberately, none
      left green-while-testing-nothing
- [ ] 0360 re-read against the result and closed or re-scoped with a reason
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Imagine + blind-spot pass 2026-09-16

**The boundary is clean in code, messy in prose.** Removable, job (a), three
contiguous blocks totalling ~240 lines: 196-199 (sourcing the trusted
`~/.claude/.env`, which on this host holds nothing but `KEYS=` and comments, so
it exists solely for job a), 201-219 (`_be_harness_keys` / `_be_explain`
bookkeeping), 296-371 (the 0361 `KEYS_EXPLAIN` drop-diagnostic), 372-510 (the
provider loop). Staying, job (b): 220-294 (project `.env` strict parse), 181-196
(`_be_is_protected_name`, called from both jobs but sharing no logic beyond the
predicate), 176-179 + 514-520 (the xtrace guard). The HEADER (lines 1-131) is
the real editing cost: ~87 lines are pure KEYS documentation and the "two .env
sources with different trust levels" framing collapses to one source. Budget for
it rather than treating this as a deletion.

**Catch the leftover:** `KEYS_EXPLAIN` sits in the protected-name denylist
(line ~190) only because of the removed 0361 diagnostic. Leaving it is precisely
the "residual inert thing that reads as still doing something" this ticket
forbids for `KEYS=`.

**The 0939 xtrace guard is NOT vestigial — keep it.** This corrects the ticket's
own earlier framing. The guard brackets the whole body including the strict-parse
loop's `export "$_be_key=$_be_val"` (line 289), which exports an already-expanded
literal from the UNTRUSTED project `.env`. Nothing in the protected-name refusal
stops a project declaring `DATABASE_PASSWORD=`; the loop exports it and `bash -x`
would trace it. Same defect class as 0939, different source of the value. Rewrite
the guard's comment to name what it now protects, and say so in the commit
message.

**Test corpus, classified.** Delete outright (pure job a): `keys_precedence`
(271 l.), `keys_protect_critical_names` (250 l.), `keys_selection_explicit`
(335 l.), `keys_selection` (198 l.). Untouched (structure-agnostic):
`tested_via_subprocess`, `test_bash_tests_are_hermetic`. **MIXED — edit, do not
delete or leave:** `project_env_parse` (drop case 5, the trusted-source
regression, and case 7b, which goes vacuous once nothing reads `$KEYS`);
`robustness` (drop case 2, CRLF on the KEYS line); `xtrace_silent` (cases 1, 2
and 3 test paths that will not exist — **and the suite goes green testing
nothing unless a new sentinel case proves the strict-parse loop does not leak a
project-`.env` value under `-x`**). That last one is this ticket's own exit
criterion biting its own newest test.

**Consumer enumeration verified independently**, not taken from the tracker:
`peer_review.py:87,94` and `skills/update-publist/SKILL.md:74-85` are still
ambient and are the two blockers. `seat-runner.sh` is genuinely already covered
by 0393 — its value comes from `--credential-env` resolved at point of use, not
from residency. No fourth consumer exists in this repo.

**Blind-spot finding, and its correction.** The pass flagged
`scripts/pipeline_keystore.py` in consuming projects (named in this file's own
header at line 78) as an out-of-repo reader of `$KEYS` that could break
silently. Checked at the call site rather than from the comment:
`climate-finance-het/scripts/pipeline_loaders.py:55` calls
`load_dotenv(BASE_DIR/.env)` and only then `apply_keys_selection()` at line 63,
so that repo populates `os.environ["KEYS"]` itself via python-dotenv and never
depends on `bash-env.sh`. **No breakage.** What remains is divergence: after
this ticket the harness abandons a mechanism a consuming project still
implements, and this file's line-78 comment claiming the two paths "agree"
becomes false. Fix the comment here; the other repo's copy is its own business.

**Author's decision, 2026-09-16:** `KEYS` is added to the protected-name
denylist, so a project `.env` cannot export it at all. Chosen over letting the
strict-parse pass it through as an ordinary string. Safe as verified above,
because python-dotenv is unaffected by this file's refusal list.

**Not a monster ticket:** ≤8 files, one sign-off unit, dependency chain explicit
in `Blocked-by` rather than hidden. The risk here is sequencing, not scope: do
not dispatch until 0943 and 0944 are MERGED, verified in the tree rather than by
the existence of their tickets.

## Exit criteria (added 2026-09-16)
- [ ] `KEYS` added to `_be_is_protected_name`, so a project `.env` cannot export
      it; a test proves the refusal fires
- [ ] `KEYS_EXPLAIN` removed from the denylist with its comment
- [ ] The xtrace guard is KEPT, its comment rewritten to name project-`.env`
      values, and a new sentinel case proves the strict-parse loop does not leak
      one under `-x`
- [ ] The line-78 comment about the Python apply path agreeing is corrected
- [ ] Each MIXED suite edited case-by-case, none left green-while-testing-nothing
